  "result": "I filled in the rule and its witness file for NRS_484B_263_o2, and the gate returned **`OK` on its first run** (5 witnesses, 9 names, composes nothing), using 1 of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_263_o2.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a road user in the vehicle aggregate, `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject is moving, and it entered or left some controlled-access region c within the merge window (`p.merge_window`) before the current moment, but not at the current moment itself.\n  - \"Entered\" means its footprint has just started to overlap c; \"left\" means the overlap has just ended.\n  - The time is measured from the latest of those two events.\n- **What it requires:** for every such region c (the obligation restates the same selection), take every other road user v that:\n  - is in both the traffic and the vehicle aggregates;\n  - is moving and is on c;\n  - has the subject ahead of it.\n\n  For each such v, the subject must not touch v, and the two must not reach their closest approach within `p.conflict_horizon` at a centre distance below `p.conflict_centre_clearance`.\n- I added no narrowings. The way I wrote \"entry or exit\" is the record's own wording, and every name the node claims is used.\n\n**The witnesses** are built on a controlled-access road with a plain approach road beside it. The subject's entry onto the controlled-access road happens at t = 2 s.\n- **forbid:** a faster car closes from 20 m behind, which is a conflict.\n- **permit:** a slower car is 400 m or more behind, so they separate.\n- **idle:** the same closing car, but judged 11–12 s after entry, past the 10 s merge window.\n- **blind:** forbid's scene with `kin.speed` masked.\n- **branch_1:** the subject alone.\n\nEvery witness only judges the moments after the recorded entry. Before that, the time since the last entry or exit is truly unknown, because one could have happened before the recording started.\n\nBefore the first gate run I sent one command that wasn't the gate command (a `--help` probe). It was blocked and never ran, so it used no gate runs; `task_result.md` records it.\n\nFiles are in `library/` under the pipeline directory:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_263_o2.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_263_o2.lean`\n- `task_result.md` (in the working directory)",
